    <detaileddescription>
<para>Caller-controlled dense vector storage for cuVS CAGRA.</para>
<para>Dimensions and row strides are in elements, with contiguous columns. Binary vectors use UInt8, and their dimension is the number of bytes, not bits. Views never own or copy their allocation. An owning <ref refid="classfaiss_1_1gpu_1_1Dataset" kindref="compound">Dataset</ref> controls the allocation&apos;s lifetime; CAGRA always borrows it. Keep the backing allocation alive and unchanged until all indexes using it and queued GPU work finish. Moving an owning <ref refid="classfaiss_1_1gpu_1_1Dataset" kindref="compound">Dataset</ref> preserves its allocation and existing borrowed views. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
